{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836310",
      "title": "Refs vs State Values",
      "sourceHash": "736fcad193cea7a270790c78d743db25ac239396b6698fd8a8d966c77ed70509",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "So refs can be pretty useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "and you will soon learn about another use case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "where refs can be useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "even if you don't connect them to HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "But before we go there, it's really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 19.15,
          "en": "to also understand the difference between refs and state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.04,
          "end": 23.13,
          "en": "because here you could ask yourself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.13,
          "end": 25.893,
          "en": "why are we using this state at all?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 30,
          "en": "Why don't we get rid of that state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30,
          "end": 32.883,
          "en": "and of that state updating function call here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "and we instead directly use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "playerName.current.value down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 41.523,
          "en": "Why don't we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.14,
          "end": 46.59,
          "en": "And the answer is because it doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.59,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "If we try to do that, you see that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.23,
          "en": "something seems to go wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.23,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "And indeed here I have an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 59.343,
          "en": "that it fails to read a property value of undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.65,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "So the problem here is that I'm trying to access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 67.8,
          "en": "this value property on the value stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.8,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "in playerName.current,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.243,
          "en": "and that playerName.current seems to be undefined here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "And the reason for that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 77.94,
          "en": "that I'm trying to output the value stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.94,
          "end": 80.07,
          "en": "in playerName.current here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.07,
          "end": 83.193,
          "en": "when the component gets rendered for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.33,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "But when that happens, this connection here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.18299999999999,
          "en": "through this ref prop won't be established yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.44,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "So in that first component render cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 96.36,
          "en": "when that component function is executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 101.223,
          "en": "playerName.current will simply be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "It's only in the next render cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 108.3,
          "en": "that it will have disconnection to this input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.3,
          "end": 111.063,
          "en": "and that we will be able to reach the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "But we could, of course, work around that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 119.88300000000001,
          "en": "by checking if playerName.current is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "So if it's not undefined, and if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "we try to output playerName.current.value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "because then we know that playerName.current is set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 134.82,
          "en": "so that this connection has been established.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 136.653,
          "en": "And otherwise we output that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "If we tweak the code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 143.103,
          "en": "and we save that the error indeed goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "But you will now also see that if I enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "and I click Set Name, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "It's cleared, but unknown entity isn't replaced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "And that is the key difference between refs and state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "It's not just that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 164.85,
          "en": "this connection doesn't exist yet initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.85,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "More importantly, it's that whenever a ref changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 173.253,
          "en": "the component function does not re-execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.15,
          "end": 177.18,
          "en": "And for a state, that's of course different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 177.18,
          "end": 178.95,
          "en": "Whenever you update state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.95,
          "end": 181.5,
          "en": "by calling that state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 184.293,
          "en": "the component function will be re-executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "And for refs, that's simply not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "So, therefore, both state and refs are important concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 195.75,
          "en": "and have their purposes in the React world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.75,
          "end": 200.43,
          "en": "State values do cause a component to be re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.43,
          "end": 204.18,
          "en": "when changed through that state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.18,
          "end": 206.64,
          "en": "and therefore state should be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 208.68,
          "en": "whenever you have values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 211.683,
          "en": "that should directly be reflected in the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.21,
          "end": 216.06,
          "en": "On the other hand, you should not use state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.06,
          "end": 219.51,
          "en": "for values that are only used behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.51,
          "end": 222.75,
          "en": "and have no direct UI impact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 224.07,
          "en": "And you'll see an example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.07,
          "end": 228.273,
          "en": "for such a value in the next lectures in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 231.15,
          "en": "Now, refs on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.15,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "do not cause a component to be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 237.84,
          "en": "The component will not be reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 240.603,
          "en": "just because the ref value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 244.86,
          "en": "But you can use refs, as I showed you before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 244.86,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "to gain direct DOM element access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 250.29,
          "en": "And you'll see another example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.29,
          "end": 252.54,
          "en": "where this can be useful later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.54,
          "end": 255.69,
          "en": "But you, of course, already see an example here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 255.69,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "where we use refs to get the value that's currently entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 260.523,
          "en": "in an input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.23,
          "end": 266.28,
          "en": "But now with that, I'll also bring back my state here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.28,
          "end": 267.96,
          "en": "because, as you now learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.96,
          "end": 271.56,
          "en": "you need that state to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.56,
          "end": 274.653,
          "en": "and to reflect the updated value on the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.97,
          "end": 279.15,
          "en": "And with that, we're back to that state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.15,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "where it works as it should,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 283.293,
          "en": "and we can now dive deeper into refs.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}